  "content": {
    "id": "p44-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Divide these polynomials and write in the form $P(x)=D(x)Q(x)+R(x)$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p44-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p44-q4-a-given",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 1,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "(3x^4-4x^3+4x-8)\\div(x^2-2)",
                  "display": false
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "p44-q4-a-scaffold",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 1,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\begin{array}{rl} &\\begin{array}{rrrrr}3x^2&&&&\\end{array}\\\\ x^2-2&\\begin{array}{|rrrrr}\\hline 3x^4&-4x^3&+0x^2&+4x&-8\\\\3x^4&&-6x^2&&\\\\\\hline \\end{array}\\end{array}",
                  "display": true
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\begin{aligned}3x^4-4x^3+4x-8&=(x^2-2)(3x^2-4x+6)\\\\&\\quad-4x+4.\\end{aligned}$",
          "worked": "Continue the supplied long division:\n$$\\begin{aligned}(3x^4-4x^3+0x^2+4x-8)-(3x^4-6x^2)&=-4x^3+6x^2+4x-8,\\\\(-4x^3+6x^2+4x-8)-(-4x^3+8x)&=6x^2-4x-8,\\\\(6x^2-4x-8)-(6x^2-12)&=-4x+4.\\end{aligned}$$\nThe quotient terms are $3x^2$, $-4x$ and $6$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}3x^4-4x^3+4x-8&=(x^2-2)(3x^2-4x+6)-4x+4.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 65
      },
      {
        "id": "p44-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$(x^3-3x^2+x+4)\\div(x^2-x)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^3-3x^2+x+4=(x^2-x)(x-2)-x+4$.",
          "worked": "Long division gives quotient terms $x$ and $-2$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}(x^3-3x^2+x+4)-(x^3-x^2)&=-2x^2+x+4,\\\\(-2x^2+x+4)-(-2x^2+2x)&=-x+4.\\end{aligned}$$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}x^3-3x^2+x+4&=(x^2-x)(x-2)-x+4.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p44-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$(x^3+x^2-7x+6)\\div(x^2+3x-1)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^3+x^2-7x+6=(x^2+3x-1)(x-2)+4$.",
          "worked": "Long division gives quotient terms $x$ and $-2$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}(x^3+x^2-7x+6)-(x^3+3x^2-x)&=-2x^2-6x+6,\\\\(-2x^2-6x+6)-(-2x^2-6x+2)&=4.\\end{aligned}$$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}x^3+x^2-7x+6&=(x^2+3x-1)(x-2)+4.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p44-q4-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$(x^4-3x^3+x^2-7x+3)\\div(x^2-4x+2)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\begin{aligned}x^4-3x^3+x^2-7x+3&=(x^2-4x+2)(x^2+x+3)\\\\&\\quad+3x-3.\\end{aligned}$",
          "worked": "Long division gives quotient terms $x^2$, $x$ and $3$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}(x^4-3x^3+x^2-7x+3)-(x^4-4x^3+2x^2)&=x^3-x^2-7x+3,\\\\(x^3-x^2-7x+3)-(x^3-4x^2+2x)&=3x^2-9x+3,\\\\(3x^2-9x+3)-(3x^2-12x+6)&=3x-3.\\end{aligned}$$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}x^4-3x^3+x^2-7x+3&=(x^2-4x+2)(x^2+x+3)+3x-3.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 80
      },
      {
        "id": "p44-q4-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$(x^3-3x^2+5x-4)\\div(x^2+2)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^3-3x^2+5x-4=(x^2+2)(x-3)+3x+2$.",
          "worked": "Long division gives quotient terms $x$ and $-3$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}(x^3-3x^2+5x-4)-(x^3+2x)&=-3x^2+3x-4,\\\\(-3x^2+3x-4)-(-3x^2-6)&=3x+2.\\end{aligned}$$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}x^3-3x^2+5x-4&=(x^2+2)(x-3)+3x+2.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p44-q4-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$(2x^3-3)\\div(2x-4)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2x^3-3=(2x-4)(x^2+2x+4)+13$.",
          "worked": "Include the missing $x^2$ and $x$ terms. Long division gives quotient terms $x^2$, $2x$ and $4$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}(2x^3+0x^2+0x-3)-(2x^3-4x^2)&=4x^2-3,\\\\(4x^2+0x-3)-(4x^2-8x)&=8x-3,\\\\(8x-3)-(8x-16)&=13.\\end{aligned}$$\n$$2x^3-3=(2x-4)(x^2+2x+4)+13.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      }
    ]
  },
